4
00:04:36.258 --> 00:04:38.051
You sure you're okay?

5
00:04:42.055 --> 00:04:44.391
Do you want me to leave
or something?

6
00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:50.856
No, stay.
I'm gonna go get some air.

7
00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:10.644
You know you got two
different shoes on, right?

8
00:06:14.815 --> 00:06:16.900
One's a little newer
than the other.

9
00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:19.319
Anything else?

10
00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.157
Thanks for stopping by.

11
00:06:58.692 --> 00:07:00.902
What the hell
did you just do?

12
00:07:04.364 --> 00:07:06.324
How did you get up there?

13
00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:37.188
Be strong, fellows.
We going, baby. Come on.

14
00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:43.361
One of us has to move on
some of that. Oh, yeah?

15
00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:46.531
Well, some of us already have.
Hi, Dory.

16
00:07:46.573 --> 00:07:49.325
Hey, Tommy. Hey, Dan!

17
00:07:49.409 --> 00:07:51.494
Looking good,
all right.

18
00:07:51.578 --> 00:07:52.662
Thanks, Trev.

19
00:07:52.745 --> 00:07:55.248
Referring to the endless array
of women, dickhead.

20
00:07:55.331 --> 00:07:59.002
How can they all be in love
with me? Exactly, how can they?

21
00:07:59.085 --> 00:08:01.004
Incoming, gentlemen.

22
00:08:01.796 --> 00:08:04.841
Oh, my sweet mama and papa.

23
00:08:04.924 --> 00:08:08.052
See that smile she gave us?
Yeah. Looked like a toothpaste ad.

24
00:08:08.136 --> 00:08:11.055
Whitest teeth
I've ever come across.

25
00:08:11.097 --> 00:08:13.933
Faster, faster!
Punch hard, punch hard.

26
00:08:14.017 --> 00:08:16.769
Heel! Good!
All right, Jensen.

27
00:08:16.853 --> 00:08:19.898
You work hard and you get
results. That's how it happens.

28
00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.615
Nice, Kyle.

29
00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:32.285
Excellent.

30
00:08:34.454 --> 00:08:37.749
Now, who else has some good
stuff to show me today, huh?

31
00:08:38.082 --> 00:08:40.960
All right, Millman. Nice.

32
00:08:41.044 --> 00:08:44.464
Tight. Lower your shoulders.
Good. Keep it tight.

33
00:08:47.634 --> 00:08:49.636
Good, good.

34
00:08:49.719 --> 00:08:53.806
I want to show you something, Coach.
Don't waste energy. Keep that mouth shut.

35
00:08:54.557 --> 00:08:55.975
Good.

36
00:08:57.935 --> 00:08:59.729
Millman. Millman!

37
00:09:12.533 --> 00:09:13.993
Sorry, Coach.

38
00:09:14.786 --> 00:09:16.704
Sorry doesn't mean anything.

39
00:09:18.539 --> 00:09:20.083
I can do this.

40
00:09:20.708 --> 00:09:22.543
I've been working on it.

41
00:09:24.337 --> 00:09:25.838
Get over here!

42
00:09:27.298 --> 00:09:30.760
Nobody on this planet can do
what you are trying to do.

43
00:09:33.513 --> 00:09:37.016
You are great up there, Danny.
You're one of the best I've seen.

44
00:09:38.267 --> 00:09:41.229
You're gonna rank even higher
than you did last year,

45
00:09:41.312 --> 00:09:44.482
and you might make it
through all the qualifiers if

46
00:09:44.524 --> 00:09:46.526
you don't
kill yourself first.

47
00:09:50.404 --> 00:09:51.906
Tommy, you're up.

48
00:09:55.993 --> 00:09:57.703
What's he trying to do?

49
00:09:57.787 --> 00:10:00.456
Three consecutive flips
before he dismounts.

50
00:10:01.374 --> 00:10:04.418
Anybody ever done that?
Nope.

51
00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:07.547
That's why
he's trying to do it.

52
00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:10.049
Thinks it's gonna make him
lord of the rings.

53
00:10:10.091 --> 00:10:13.803
Only, with Middleman, it's where he tries
to tear both arms out of their sockets.

54
00:10:13.886 --> 00:10:17.765
All right, the next qualifying
heat is six weeks from today,

55
00:10:17.848 --> 00:10:19.558
and you know what I say.

56
00:10:19.642 --> 00:10:21.185
Don't think
this is gonna happen

57
00:10:21.269 --> 00:10:24.689
just 'cause you're pretty
and can do a handstand.

58
00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.024
You think I'm kidding?

59
00:10:27.066 --> 00:10:30.820
And I've got footage of your
competition you need to see again.

60
00:11:08.441 --> 00:11:10.443
Help you with something?

61
00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:19.702
You can tell me
how you did it.

62
00:11:23.539 --> 00:11:25.541
You like things explained.

63
00:11:28.252 --> 00:11:29.503
Don't you?

64
00:11:37.636 --> 00:11:39.388
How we doing tonight?

65
00:11:41.682 --> 00:11:43.225
Look.

66
00:11:43.309 --> 00:11:47.021
That roof's gotta be at
least 10, maybe 12 feet high.

67
00:11:48.814 --> 00:11:51.734
No human can make a vertical
leap over four or five feet, tops.

68
00:11:51.817 --> 00:11:53.485
I know. I'm a gymnast.

69
00:11:55.571 --> 00:11:59.700
Toughest men's sport in the
world. Most people don't know that.

70
00:11:59.783 --> 00:12:03.621
The Spartans of ancient Greece
were gymnasts, too.

71
00:12:03.662 --> 00:12:05.789
They vaulted over bulls.

72
00:12:05.873 --> 00:12:08.417
Trained their elite warriors
that way.

73
00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.169
Did you know that?

74
00:12:11.629 --> 00:12:15.507
I know more than you think. And
you think more than you know.

75
00:12:16.008 --> 00:12:18.135
But knowledge is
not the same as wisdom.

76
00:12:18.218 --> 00:12:20.346
Yeah? What's the difference?

77
00:12:21.138 --> 00:12:24.141
You know how to clean a
windshield, right? Yeah.

78
00:12:24.224 --> 00:12:25.976
Wisdom is doing it.

79
00:12:32.524 --> 00:12:36.153
I train seven days a week,
50 weeks out of the year.

80
00:12:36.862 --> 00:12:39.073
Why so much?
Are you serious?

81
00:12:41.033 --> 00:12:43.285
I am a heartbeat away
from qualifying.

82
00:12:43.369 --> 00:12:44.995
Qualifying for what?

83
00:12:47.373 --> 00:12:49.500
You watch the Olympics?
No.

84
00:12:51.543 --> 00:12:53.170
Thanks for stopping by.

85
00:12:54.713 --> 00:12:57.174
Look, even as good as I am,

86
00:12:59.176 --> 00:13:02.679
I gotta do everything I can
to make sure that I qualify.

87
00:13:03.222 --> 00:13:07.518
There's a lot you'd have to know before
you could understand what you saw.

88
00:13:09.228 --> 00:13:12.189
Go. Ask me.
Ask me something.

89
00:13:13.357 --> 00:13:14.942
Ask me anything.

90
00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.072
Are you happy?

91
00:13:23.492 --> 00:13:25.911
You said
I could ask you anything.

92
00:13:26.954 --> 00:13:29.248
What does happy
have to do with anything?

93
00:13:29.331 --> 00:13:30.666
Everything.

94
00:13:30.749 --> 00:13:32.709
My dad's got plenty of cash,

95
00:13:33.585 --> 00:13:36.213
school's kind of a breeze,
I get straight A's.

96
00:13:37.297 --> 00:13:39.091
I got great friends,
I'm in great shape,

97
00:13:39.174 --> 00:13:42.219
and I only sleep alone
when I absolutely want to.

98
00:13:42.302 --> 00:13:44.513
So why can't you
sleep at night?

99
00:13:46.682 --> 00:13:49.977
Yesterday, you came here
at 3:00 a. m. Now, tonight.

100
00:13:50.435 --> 00:13:52.354
That's two nights in a row.

101
00:13:52.437 --> 00:13:55.565
What are you? Some kind of a Quickie
Mart philosopher or something like that?

102
00:13:55.607 --> 00:13:56.775
You need some philosophy?

103
00:13:56.858 --> 00:13:59.778
No, thanks, Socrates.
I get enough at school.

104
00:14:01.405 --> 00:14:02.906
Last question.

105
00:14:03.615 --> 00:14:07.160
If you don't make the Olympic
team, what will you do?

106
00:14:11.456 --> 00:14:13.083
If I don't what?

107
00:14:13.125 --> 00:14:14.835
You must have thought
about it.

108
00:14:14.918 --> 00:14:16.628
What the hell
are you talking about?

109
00:14:16.712 --> 00:14:18.463
What's the problem?

110
00:14:21.508 --> 00:14:23.969
I don't even know
what I'm doing here.

111
00:14:25.429 --> 00:14:28.807
You're a freak. And I don't
need you freaking me out.

112
00:14:34.187 --> 00:14:36.356
Thirteen.

113
00:14:38.942 --> 00:14:41.236
Fourteen.

114
00:14:41.319 --> 00:14:43.655
Your exit sign's lit, Middleman.

115
00:14:47.367 --> 00:14:49.411
Fifteen.

116
00:14:52.122 --> 00:14:53.915
Sixteen.

117
00:14:53.999 --> 00:14:57.627
Hey, there, beautiful thing.
So, this is what you do for fun.

118
00:15:01.006 --> 00:15:02.883
Seventeen.

119
00:15:02.966 --> 00:15:04.634
Eighteen.

120
00:15:09.723 --> 00:15:12.309
Did I pick up that maybe you and
Dory hooked up the other night?

121
00:15:12.392 --> 00:15:14.186
Come on, Dan-o.
It's all you.

122
00:15:16.688 --> 00:15:18.148
Nineteen.

123
00:15:18.648 --> 00:15:20.817
She told you that?
Is it true?

124
00:15:25.113 --> 00:15:27.324
We're supposed to be friends,
man.

125
00:15:30.577 --> 00:15:32.996
What does
that mean, exactly?

126
00:15:33.038 --> 00:15:36.499
It means you're a jerk who
treats his friends like dirt.

127
00:15:36.541 --> 00:15:38.335
Somebody grab my beers.

128
00:15:42.339 --> 00:15:44.007
Somebody grab mine!

129
00:15:49.387 --> 00:15:50.889
Hey! Hey! Hey!

130
00:15:53.391 --> 00:15:54.601
Come on, guys.

131
00:15:54.684 --> 00:15:56.645
Hey, Dan, what's the matter
