162
00:19:28.439 --> 00:19:30.232
Japanese style, huh?

163
00:19:41.327 --> 00:19:43.579
So you know Socrates?

164
00:19:43.662 --> 00:19:45.915
Is that what you call him?

165
00:19:45.956 --> 00:19:48.459
I bet he loves that.

166
00:19:48.542 --> 00:19:50.669
You eat here with him
every night?

167
00:19:50.753 --> 00:19:53.005
Actually,
I think one's for you.

168
00:19:56.759 --> 00:19:58.469
I see you've met Joy.

169
00:19:58.552 --> 00:20:00.763
Hey, big Buddha.
Hi, little Buddha.

170
00:20:01.722 --> 00:20:03.432
Joy, this is Dan.

171
00:20:04.475 --> 00:20:05.935
We met.

172
00:20:05.976 --> 00:20:07.978
Socrates.
Socrates.

173
00:20:09.605 --> 00:20:10.981
Bon appétit.

174
00:20:19.323 --> 00:20:20.950
You look hungry.

175
00:20:29.333 --> 00:20:30.918
Joy do all that?

176
00:20:42.096 --> 00:20:43.889
She live around here?

177
00:20:46.392 --> 00:20:48.394
She related to you
or something?

178
00:20:48.477 --> 00:20:51.313
You need to start asking
better questions.

179
00:21:03.784 --> 00:21:04.994
What?

180
00:21:05.077 --> 00:21:07.705
Slow down.
You might taste something.

181
00:21:11.333 --> 00:21:14.586
You sure got a lot of rules
about stuff, don't you?

182
00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:18.841
Not rules. Things I've learned
from my own life experience.

183
00:21:20.843 --> 00:21:23.637
That's why I'd say
your eating is sloppy.

184
00:21:25.055 --> 00:21:26.932
Who cares?
You do.

185
00:21:27.891 --> 00:21:30.018
That's the difference
between us, Dan.

186
00:21:30.102 --> 00:21:33.355
You practice gymnastics.
I practice everything.

187
00:21:34.857 --> 00:21:37.151
If I was your trainer,
no meat.

188
00:21:38.569 --> 00:21:40.571
Seriously?
None.

189
00:21:42.656 --> 00:21:44.616
I could probably
handle that.

190
00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:47.703
No TV, no alcohol,
no drugs and no sex.

191
00:21:47.786 --> 00:21:50.956
And that's why I'm glad
you're not my trainer.

192
00:21:51.039 --> 00:21:55.210
So, this diet and your training
are making you all you can be?

193
00:21:56.003 --> 00:21:57.921
Absolutely.

194
00:21:57.963 --> 00:22:01.717
So, how long
can you stand like this?

195
00:22:04.595 --> 00:22:06.096
Name it.

196
00:22:06.138 --> 00:22:08.599
Five minutes. On the table.
Done.

197
00:22:14.813 --> 00:22:16.648
You move so much as a muscle,

198
00:22:16.732 --> 00:22:19.234
and I get to call you Jack
for the rest of the night.

199
00:22:19.318 --> 00:22:21.570
Jack?
Short for jackass.

200
00:23:09.493 --> 00:23:11.078
What time is it?

201
00:23:13.997 --> 00:23:15.832
What time is it?

202
00:23:21.463 --> 00:23:23.215
What time

203
00:23:23.298 --> 00:23:24.633
is

204
00:23:24.674 --> 00:23:26.009
it?

205
00:23:29.679 --> 00:23:30.972
What

206
00:23:31.014 --> 00:23:32.724
time

207
00:23:32.808 --> 00:23:33.767
is...

208
00:23:38.563 --> 00:23:40.232
My son, Jack.

209
00:23:48.782 --> 00:23:50.700
Thanks for stopping by.

210
00:23:52.869 --> 00:23:55.914
Everyone tells you what to do
and what's good for you.

211
00:23:55.997 --> 00:23:58.458
They don't want you
to find your own answers.

212
00:23:58.542 --> 00:24:00.794
They want you
to believe theirs.

213
00:24:02.379 --> 00:24:05.215
And let me guess.
You want me to believe yours.

214
00:24:05.298 --> 00:24:06.716
No.

215
00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:10.679
I want you to stop gathering
information from outside yourself

216
00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:13.473
and start gathering it
from the inside.

217
00:24:15.517 --> 00:24:17.686
What are you, part of
some cult or something?

218
00:24:17.769 --> 00:24:20.689
People are afraid
of what's inside,

219
00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:24.276
and that's the only place they're
ever gonna find what they need.

220
00:24:25.902 --> 00:24:27.862
Why can't you sleep?

221
00:24:27.904 --> 00:24:31.032
Is it because,
maybe, late at night,

222
00:24:31.116 --> 00:24:34.369
when all the noise dies down and
you're lying there in the bed,

223
00:24:34.452 --> 00:24:38.581
and there's nobody around but you,
then, maybe, you get a little scared?

224
00:24:41.876 --> 00:24:44.838
Scared because suddenly
everything feels so

225
00:24:46.631 --> 00:24:48.091
empty.

226
00:24:52.679 --> 00:24:57.308
You tell me you want to be more than
just someone who gets up on those rings

227
00:24:57.392 --> 00:25:00.562
and performs
a well-practiced stunt or two.

228
00:25:02.856 --> 00:25:05.650
You tell me
you want to be someone

229
00:25:05.733 --> 00:25:09.070
who uses his mind and his body

230
00:25:09.154 --> 00:25:12.949
in ways that most people would
never have the courage to,

231
00:25:15.034 --> 00:25:17.370
and I will train you, Dan,

232
00:25:18.955 --> 00:25:20.999
to be a real warrior.

233
00:25:56.743 --> 00:25:58.202
Is he all right?

234
00:26:02.332 --> 00:26:04.083
What's going on?

235
00:26:04.167 --> 00:26:06.419
Kyle. He took a bad fall.

236
00:26:06.502 --> 00:26:08.338
It's fine. I'm fine.

237
00:26:11.674 --> 00:26:13.301
It might be broken.
No.

238
00:26:13.384 --> 00:26:14.886
We'll need an x-ray.
No.

239
00:26:14.969 --> 00:26:17.263
It's all right, Kyle. It's
all right. It's all right.

240
00:26:17.347 --> 00:26:19.140
I mean it, Coach.
I know.

241
00:26:19.223 --> 00:26:20.350
It doesn't feel like a break.

242
00:26:20.433 --> 00:26:22.143
They're just gonna have
a look at it, that's all.

243
00:26:22.185 --> 00:26:24.020
I don't need it looked at.

244
00:26:26.356 --> 00:26:28.107
And I said you did.

245
00:26:30.860 --> 00:26:32.153
Let's go.

246
00:26:34.197 --> 00:26:37.033
Put it in a sling.
I don't need a sling.

247
00:26:43.039 --> 00:26:45.541
Rider down, man.
Bad break.

248
00:26:45.625 --> 00:26:48.878
You don't know that.
It could be a sprain.

249
00:26:48.961 --> 00:26:52.965
I mean, he's a casualty,
Tommy-boy. He's our best horse man.

250
00:26:54.050 --> 00:26:56.177
Where do you think
that leaves us, huh?

251
00:26:56.260 --> 00:26:57.553
Trevor, get off that thing.

252
00:26:57.637 --> 00:26:59.430
Or what?
Like you don't want it?

253
00:26:59.514 --> 00:27:01.682
Except you suck
at the pommel horse, Middleman.

254
00:27:01.766 --> 00:27:04.519
I just never focused on it.

255
00:27:04.602 --> 00:27:07.438
That's 'cause you got
one big show and only one.

256
00:27:07.522 --> 00:27:08.981
Lord of the rings.

257
00:27:09.065 --> 00:27:10.691
Yeah? Want to see
what I can do?

258
00:27:10.733 --> 00:27:12.527
Don't embarrass yourself.
Go play, little boy.

259
00:27:12.568 --> 00:27:15.905
Jesus Christ, did you both
just see them take Kyle away?

260
00:27:19.909 --> 00:27:22.370
I mean, Jesus,
what if he's done?

261
00:27:22.453 --> 00:27:26.832
Don't get in my face about it, all right?
Jesus, go hold his hand if you want to.

262
00:27:40.930 --> 00:27:43.557
Sometimes,
I don't like myself very much.

263
00:27:46.269 --> 00:27:50.231
My first thought was about how maybe
Kyle's fall could work out for me.

264
00:27:53.484 --> 00:27:55.403
People are not their thoughts.

265
00:27:55.444 --> 00:27:59.532
They think they are and it
brings them all kinds of sadness.

266
00:28:01.242 --> 00:28:02.994
Toss me that wrench.

267
00:28:04.495 --> 00:28:06.288
I'm not what I think?

268
00:28:07.873 --> 00:28:09.333
Of course not.

269
00:28:15.631 --> 00:28:17.049
The five-eighths.

270
00:28:30.479 --> 00:28:32.606
The mind is just
a reflex organ.

271
00:28:32.648 --> 00:28:35.151
It reacts to everything.

272
00:28:35.234 --> 00:28:39.238
Fills your head with millions
of random thoughts a day.

273
00:28:39.321 --> 00:28:41.824
None of those thoughts
reveal any more about you

274
00:28:41.907 --> 00:28:45.786
than a freckle does
at the end of your nose.

275
00:28:52.668 --> 00:28:54.628
Take a swing at me.
What?

276
00:28:59.341 --> 00:29:00.676
What are you doing?

277
00:29:00.759 --> 00:29:03.804
Come on. 10 bucks if you
can slap me on the cheek.

278
00:29:08.017 --> 00:29:09.977
Come on. Take a shot.

279
00:29:10.060 --> 00:29:12.855
Knock it off, man.
I don't want to hit you.

280
00:29:12.938 --> 00:29:14.607
You don't want to hit me?

281
00:29:19.570 --> 00:29:21.572
I don't want to hurt you.

282
00:29:22.740 --> 00:29:25.784
I guess I'll just have to
keep slapping you then.

283
00:29:35.628 --> 00:29:39.381
Did you notice how the right
leverage can be very effective?

284
00:29:47.806 --> 00:29:49.850
What if I were to tell you

285
00:29:51.393 --> 00:29:54.897
that's what your training,
even your life, is about?

286
00:29:56.190 --> 00:29:59.860
Developing the wisdom
to apply the right leverage

287
00:29:59.943 --> 00:30:02.571
in the right place,
at the right time.

288
00:30:03.614 --> 00:30:06.367
Take out the trash.
You take out the trash.

289
00:30:07.201 --> 00:30:08.994
The trash is up here.

290
00:30:10.370 --> 00:30:12.790
That's the first part
of your training,

291
00:30:12.873 --> 00:30:16.210
learning to throw out everything
you don't need in here.

292
00:30:22.591 --> 00:30:23.717
How?

293
00:30:24.551 --> 00:30:27.846
Meet me tomorrow on campus.

294
00:30:27.930 --> 00:30:30.766
Strawberry Creek bridge.

295
00:30:32.184 --> 00:30:34.394
Where the hell are you going?
Poli-sci. Where are you going?

296
00:30:34.478 --> 00:30:37.397
I'm going to pommel horse
try-outs.

297
00:30:37.439 --> 00:30:38.482
I forgot.

298
00:30:38.565 --> 00:30:41.235
Less than an hour.
Hey, hey! Wait up.

299
00:30:41.318 --> 00:30:44.029
Tell them to hold up
for me, all right? What?

300
00:30:52.955 --> 00:30:54.081
Soc!

301
00:30:56.542 --> 00:30:57.626
Soc!

302
00:31:00.504 --> 00:31:04.049
Listen.
I totally forgot about this.

303
00:31:04.132 --> 00:31:05.968
Now, I got this thing
at the gym.

304
00:31:06.051 --> 00:31:08.929
It's pretty important.
Can we make this quick?

305
00:31:09.972 --> 00:31:11.098
Sure.

306
00:31:22.276 --> 00:31:23.443
Hey!

307
00:31:27.864 --> 00:31:30.867
Hey! I'm talking to you.

308
00:31:33.328 --> 00:31:35.956
What the hell is wrong with you?
You said you were in a hurry.

309
00:31:35.998 --> 00:31:38.291
So you pushed me off the
bridge? I emptied your mind.

310
00:31:38.375 --> 00:31:39.668
You what?
I emptied...

311
00:31:39.751 --> 00:31:42.087
No, you didn't.
You threw me into the river.

312
00:31:42.170 --> 00:31:44.589
And while you were falling, tell
me, Dan, what were you thinking of?

313
00:31:44.673 --> 00:31:45.716
I don't know!

314
00:31:45.799 --> 00:31:47.175
Were you thinking about school? No!

315
00:31:47.259 --> 00:31:48.468
Grocery shopping?
No!

316
00:31:48.510 --> 00:31:50.887
This thing you had to
hurry off to? No! I was...

317
00:31:50.971 --> 00:31:52.264
The present.

318
00:31:52.347 --> 00:31:55.267
Devoted 100% to the experience
you were having.

319
00:31:55.350 --> 00:31:56.977
You even had a word for it.

320
00:32:00.522 --> 00:32:03.150
You're out of your mind.
You know that?

321
00:32:03.608 --> 00:32:06.069
It's taken
a lifetime of practice.

322
00:32:12.951 --> 00:32:15.537
We want you
out of your mind, too, Dan.

323
00:32:19.541 --> 00:32:22.043
What is that you do?

324
00:32:22.127 --> 00:32:24.379
Some kind of
martial arts move?

325
00:32:25.338 --> 00:32:29.342
I didn't see it coming.
You weren't paying attention.

326
00:32:29.426 --> 00:32:33.471
Even now you're not.
Your mind's filling up again.

327
00:32:33.555 --> 00:32:36.474
You're missing out
on everything that's going on.

328
00:32:36.558 --> 00:32:38.560
There's nothing going on.

329
00:33:28.026 --> 00:33:30.445
There's never
nothing going on.

330
00:33:35.784 --> 00:33:37.786
Take out the trash, Dan.

331
00:33:38.787 --> 00:33:43.249
The trash is anything that is keeping
you from the only thing that matters,

332
00:33:44.209 --> 00:33:45.585
this moment.

333
00:33:46.294 --> 00:33:47.420
Here.

334
00:33:48.004 --> 00:33:49.089
Now.

335
00:33:55.178 --> 00:33:57.597
And when you truly are
in the here and now,

336
00:33:57.639 --> 00:34:02.143
you'll be amazed at what you can
do and how well you can do it.

337
00:34:07.398 --> 00:34:11.069
Until we know more about Kyle,
we need the horse covered, so...

338
00:34:12.195 --> 00:34:15.156
Anybody who wants
a shot at it, gets a shot.

339
00:34:18.409 --> 00:34:19.786
Where's Millman?

340
00:35:16.801 --> 00:35:19.554
All right,
next man up. Trev?

341
00:35:19.637 --> 00:35:22.598
You know I'm superstitious,
Coach. I gotta go last.

342
00:35:22.682 --> 00:35:24.016
I'll go.

343
00:35:30.440 --> 00:35:31.774
All right.

344
00:37:16.128 --> 00:37:20.299
Millman, where the hell
did that come from?

345
00:37:35.731 --> 00:37:36.816
Soc!

346
00:37:36.857 --> 00:37:40.819
Hot damn! I wish you could've
been there. You would've loved it!

347
00:37:41.570 --> 00:37:43.322
I used your trick.

348
00:37:43.405 --> 00:37:47.368
I used your mind trick and it worked.
It totally worked. I was awesome.

349
00:37:49.328 --> 00:37:54.083
It's not a trick. Yeah, well,
whatever it is, I used it.

350
00:37:54.833 --> 00:37:57.419
I took out the trash,
and I mean Trev?

351
00:37:57.503 --> 00:37:59.838
Trev's the one guy
I'm always going up against.

352
00:37:59.880 --> 00:38:02.883
You should have seen me.
I demolished the guy.

353
00:38:04.218 --> 00:38:07.846
You know, I wasn't worried
about what did happen,

354
00:38:07.888 --> 00:38:09.890
or what might happen,
what could happen.

355
00:38:09.932 --> 00:38:13.769
I just got up there
and I cleared my mind.

356
00:38:16.730 --> 00:38:18.482
And I was flawless.

357
00:38:22.361 --> 00:38:25.823
Listen, I'm jumping in
with both feet. All right?

358
00:38:25.906 --> 00:38:30.995
Whatever you tell me to do, I'm gonna do.
No beer, no meat, no girls, no problem.

359
00:38:31.078 --> 00:38:34.498
How long did you stay
that way, clear and flawless?

360
00:38:35.874 --> 00:38:38.919
"I demolished that guy.
You should have seen me. "

361
00:38:41.839 --> 00:38:43.549
You're in the past.

362
00:38:45.759 --> 00:38:47.052
Gloating.

363
00:38:47.928 --> 00:38:50.139
You're not in the now, living.

364
00:38:52.182 --> 00:38:54.393
You haven't learned anything.

365
00:38:57.438 --> 00:39:00.816
Go home.
Training's over for tonight.

366
00:39:03.902 --> 00:39:05.362
Wait a minute.

367
00:39:12.619 --> 00:39:14.079
Wait a minute.

368
00:39:15.789 --> 00:39:17.374
Go home, I said.

369
00:40:35.702 --> 00:40:36.995
Hey, Dan.

370
00:41:39.015 --> 00:41:42.519
Why do we have to be all the way up
here, where we could kill ourselves?

371
00:41:42.602 --> 00:41:44.562
I was hoping
you could tell me.

372
00:41:45.772 --> 00:41:46.940
God!

373
00:41:47.023 --> 00:41:48.900
What do I keep trying for?

374
00:41:51.152 --> 00:41:53.154
I'll never make this cut.

375
00:41:56.199 --> 00:41:58.076
Dad was right.

376
00:41:58.118 --> 00:42:01.746
I'm gonna make him right if
I don't find a way to do this.

377
00:42:03.123 --> 00:42:06.251
Will I ever forgive myself
if I don't make this cut?

378
00:42:06.334 --> 00:42:08.002
Where the hell is Millman?

379
00:42:08.086 --> 00:42:11.089
Too good to show up
for practice, now, I guess.

380
00:42:11.172 --> 00:42:14.551
I don't know how to handle these
kids. What do I say to them?

381
00:42:14.634 --> 00:42:17.971
They're talking,
but their lips aren't moving.

382
00:42:19.806 --> 00:42:22.684
I'm not their mother.
I'm their coach.

383
00:42:22.767 --> 00:42:24.894
Coach thinks
I'm worthless.

384
00:42:25.478 --> 00:42:27.021
I am worthless.

385
00:42:28.440 --> 00:42:30.608
I'm a worthless piece of shit

386
00:42:30.650 --> 00:42:33.153
and Millman's always
gonna be better than me.

387
00:42:33.194 --> 00:42:35.155
Am I reading their minds?

388
00:42:35.238 --> 00:42:38.950
Maybe you just never really
listened to them before.

389
00:42:38.992 --> 00:42:42.745
I've only got four qualifiers
left. I've got to get new mats.

390
00:42:42.829 --> 00:42:45.832
I can't stick this double double.
My line's not straight on the bar.

391
00:42:45.915 --> 00:42:48.376
I'm such a worthless
piece of shit.

392
00:42:52.297 --> 00:42:56.176
You gotta be doing this.
Otherwise I'm losing my mind.

393
00:42:56.259 --> 00:43:00.638
Sometimes you have to lose your
mind before you come to your senses.

394
00:43:02.015 --> 00:43:03.349
Millman!

395
00:43:05.810 --> 00:43:07.812
It's about time you showed up.

396
00:43:08.980 --> 00:43:10.857
Thanks for joining us.

397
00:43:54.734 --> 00:43:56.361
Go home, I said.

398
00:44:15.797 --> 00:44:17.882
What did you just do to me?

399
00:44:22.929 --> 00:44:26.182
You have to be strong
if you're gonna do this, Dan.

400
00:44:27.099 --> 00:44:29.018
What did you do?

401
00:44:29.101 --> 00:44:32.980
Where I'm gonna take you, some
of the things I'm gonna show you,

402
00:44:34.524 --> 00:44:36.609
you're gonna need strength.

403
00:44:37.985 --> 00:44:40.404
And you're gonna need
to trust me.

404
00:44:50.206 --> 00:44:52.250
So it's hot as hell,
and this penguin,

405
00:44:52.333 --> 00:44:55.461
he's pushing his broken-down
car past the 31 flavors.

406
00:44:55.544 --> 00:44:58.256
So, suddenly he's practically
burying his face in a large vanilla

407
00:44:58.339 --> 00:45:00.049
when he sees
a service station.

408
00:45:00.132 --> 00:45:02.927
So he goes over, the mechanic
opens up the hood and says,

409
00:45:02.969 --> 00:45:06.055
"Looks to me
like you've blown a seal. "

410
00:45:06.138 --> 00:45:10.142
The penguin wipes his mouth and says,
"Hey, screw you! It's ice cream. "

411
00:45:15.314 --> 00:45:17.650
What's up, Tommy?
Hey, Trev.

412
00:45:18.985 --> 00:45:21.737
Hey, what's up with
the rabbit chow, Middleman?

413
00:45:27.910 --> 00:45:29.620
All right, I got another one.

414
00:45:29.704 --> 00:45:33.666
A man, a duck and a big-breasted
nun walk into a bar, right?

415
00:45:33.749 --> 00:45:36.210
So, this old guy
did this high jump.

416
00:45:39.422 --> 00:45:41.382
Did this really high jump.

417
00:45:42.383 --> 00:45:43.634
And?

418
00:45:45.845 --> 00:45:48.305
I'm kind of doing
what he tells me

419
00:45:49.348 --> 00:45:51.642
so I can find out
how he did it.

420
00:45:51.725 --> 00:45:52.935
Wait a minute.

421
00:45:53.018 --> 00:45:55.813
You're letting somebody
else coach you? No.

422
00:45:56.856 --> 00:46:00.151
Well, what's he doing to you?
'Cause you look like crap.

423
00:46:00.192 --> 00:46:01.569
I don't know.

424
00:46:04.363 --> 00:46:06.866
I don't know
what he's doing to me.

425
00:46:14.874 --> 00:46:17.126
You better get away from it,
Middleman.

426
00:46:17.209 --> 00:46:21.630
We got qualifiers in four weeks and you're
looking like a worthless piece of shit.

427
00:46:36.061 --> 00:46:37.146
Hey!

428
00:46:38.731 --> 00:46:40.316
Joy, right?
Mmm-hmm.

429
00:46:41.191 --> 00:46:43.819
I need to talk to you
about our mutual friend.

430
00:46:44.528 --> 00:46:45.779
Socrates?

431
00:46:47.156 --> 00:46:50.409
If he didn't tell you his
name, you won't get it from me.

432
00:46:50.492 --> 00:46:52.953
Yeah, why didn't he tell me?

433
00:46:53.037 --> 00:46:55.539
I mean, I don't know anything
about the guy.

434
00:46:57.333 --> 00:46:59.001
I'm serious.

435
00:46:59.084 --> 00:47:02.671
All right? He's supposed to be making
me stronger, making my life better.

436
00:47:02.755 --> 00:47:04.381
It's just the opposite.

437
00:47:05.924 --> 00:47:07.426
What's he doing?

438
00:47:08.135 --> 00:47:10.179
What are you worried about?

439
00:47:10.763 --> 00:47:13.557
I want to know
who I'm dealing with here.

440
00:48:24.211 --> 00:48:26.630
Come on, come on.
Tight. Keep it tight, Danny!

441
00:48:26.672 --> 00:48:29.341
No! No, you're shaking!
You're shaking!

442
00:48:30.842 --> 00:48:33.470
What the hell
are you doing up there?

443
00:48:35.681 --> 00:48:38.809
Yeah, I'm off today.

444
00:48:38.892 --> 00:48:40.310
Oh. You're off, huh?

445
00:48:40.394 --> 00:48:42.729
Well, you've been off for
one hell of a streak, Millman.

446
00:48:42.813 --> 00:48:46.108
First you're a dream on the horse and
now you can barely stand up straight.

447
00:48:46.191 --> 00:48:47.275
Huh?

448
00:48:48.443 --> 00:48:52.572
Next time you're tired, go take a
nap instead of coming to practice.

449
00:49:00.664 --> 00:49:02.666
Ike, your key?
Yep, all right.

450
00:49:12.968 --> 00:49:14.177
Voyeur.

451
00:49:14.886 --> 00:49:16.596
How we doing tonight?

452
00:49:16.680 --> 00:49:18.181
How am I doing?

453
00:49:18.974 --> 00:49:21.852
I'm tired, I'm hungry
and I'm horny.

454
00:49:21.935 --> 00:49:23.603
How are you doing?

455
00:49:26.481 --> 00:49:28.608
I need some answers tonight.

456
00:49:30.402 --> 00:49:32.195
I need to know that this...

457
00:49:32.237 --> 00:49:36.533
That this is all going somewhere,
and I need to know it right now.

458
00:49:36.616 --> 00:49:40.745
I mean, what kind of a warrior trains
by sitting around scrubbing toilets?

459
00:49:40.829 --> 00:49:43.790
When you become a warrior, you
learn to meditate in every action.

460
00:49:43.874 --> 00:49:46.835
Scrubbing toilets?
Letting go of attachments.

461
00:49:47.586 --> 00:49:49.212
Like your pride.

462
00:49:49.254 --> 00:49:51.882
Giving up your addictions. Yeah,
name one thing I'm addicted to.

463
00:49:51.965 --> 00:49:55.427
Talking.
Especially interrupting.

464
00:49:55.510 --> 00:49:58.013
Knowing everything,
when in fact you know nothing.

465
00:49:58.096 --> 00:50:01.600
You really think that this is going
to expand my awareness of anything?

466
00:50:01.683 --> 00:50:04.895
My game is off! My coach
probably thinks that I'm on drugs,

467
00:50:04.978 --> 00:50:06.521
and I'm thinking...

468
00:50:08.940 --> 00:50:11.943
I just don't have any more
time for you right now.

469
00:50:12.944 --> 00:50:15.405
All you have is right now,
Jack.

470
00:50:18.617 --> 00:50:20.827
Did you just call me
a jackass again?

471
00:50:22.537 --> 00:50:25.707
'Cause, you know, I'm really starting
to wonder how someone with the life

472
00:50:25.790 --> 00:50:29.085
that you've managed to put
together can teach me anything.

473
00:50:30.086 --> 00:50:32.255
I mean, are you really happy?

474
00:50:33.298 --> 00:50:36.384
Maybe you're just a case of someone
who, not having made much of themselves,

475
00:50:36.468 --> 00:50:39.471
says that the world is lost and
all these things don't matter.

476
00:50:39.554 --> 00:50:43.308
Be happy with less, right? Less
than what? Less than nothing?

477
00:50:43.391 --> 00:50:46.770
I call you a jackass
when you act like a jackass.

478
00:50:46.853 --> 00:50:49.856
Like now, Dan, when you're
letting your emotions control you.

479
00:50:49.939 --> 00:50:52.776
This isn't emotion!
This is common sense!

480
00:50:54.903 --> 00:50:58.156
You know what?
Let me tell you something,

481
00:50:58.239 --> 00:51:00.450
whatever your name really is.

482
00:51:02.285 --> 00:51:05.246
When I get what I want,
I'll be happy.

483
00:51:06.623 --> 00:51:10.460
For real and forever and
anything else I say it'll be.

484
00:51:11.961 --> 00:51:13.713
'Cause I will make it happen.

485
00:51:44.786 --> 00:51:47.872
Three, two, one!

486
00:51:55.713 --> 00:51:58.216
Drink! Drink! Drink!

487
00:51:59.217 --> 00:52:00.760
Danny, good.

488
00:52:01.552 --> 00:52:02.929
That's it, Danny.

489
00:52:03.012 --> 00:52:04.180
Steady.

490
00:52:05.723 --> 00:52:09.060
Good. All right, come on!
Bring it home!

491
00:52:17.193 --> 00:52:20.363
That's what I remember about
you, Millman! You were good.

492
00:52:28.287 --> 00:52:29.789
I needed this.

493
00:52:30.289 --> 00:52:31.958
Needed to escape.

494
00:52:33.000 --> 00:52:36.587
Lucky me.
Yeah, and lucky me.

495
00:52:36.671 --> 00:52:39.173
You guys
are in such great shape.

496
00:52:39.966 --> 00:52:42.468
So if I wasn't
in such great shape,

497
00:52:43.386 --> 00:52:46.597
wasn't on the gymnastics team,
just had a regular body,

498
00:52:46.681 --> 00:52:48.349
you wouldn't be into me?

499
00:52:48.433 --> 00:52:51.394
If I didn't have this body,
would you be into me?

500
00:54:55.434 --> 00:54:57.019
Hey, Middleman.

501
00:54:58.896 --> 00:55:00.439
I don't know what to say.

502
00:55:00.523 --> 00:55:01.815
Hey.

503
00:55:02.858 --> 00:55:04.818
Got the whole team here.

504
00:55:04.902 --> 00:55:08.405
You ran a red light, man.
Can you believe that?

505
00:55:08.489 --> 00:55:10.074
You gotta get better, man,
'cause...

506
00:55:10.157 --> 00:55:11.283
You ran a red light.

507
00:55:11.367 --> 00:55:13.077
...whose ass
am I gonna kick at practice?

508
00:55:13.160 --> 00:55:15.496
Don't waste your energy.
Keep that mouth shut.

509
00:55:15.579 --> 00:55:16.872
Dan?

510
00:55:59.456 --> 00:56:00.541
Dan?

511
00:56:12.490 --> 00:56:15.493
I hear your folks are waiting
down in the cafeteria.

512
00:56:15.577 --> 00:56:17.954
I don't want my folks.

513
00:56:18.037 --> 00:56:20.373
I want to know
what's going on.

514
00:56:20.456 --> 00:56:22.834
I'm gonna tell you, but
your parents will probably...

515
00:56:22.917 --> 00:56:26.129
I don't need anyone
to hold my hand right now.

516
00:56:26.212 --> 00:56:28.923
My leg is in a cast.
When does it come off?

517
00:56:29.007 --> 00:56:32.260
Your leg didn't just break,
Dan.

518
00:56:32.343 --> 00:56:33.761
It shattered.

519
00:56:35.555 --> 00:56:38.558
You fractured your femur
in 17 different pieces.

520
00:56:40.435 --> 00:56:44.480
We had to take bone from your hip and
pin it to your leg with a steel rod.

521
00:56:48.693 --> 00:56:50.820
How long for it to come out?

522
00:56:53.114 --> 00:56:54.824
It doesn't come out.

523
00:56:56.868 --> 00:56:59.328
Now, in a few months, you'll be
able to start the rehab process.

524
00:56:59.412 --> 00:57:01.748
You can talk to your
physical therapist,

525
00:57:02.832 --> 00:57:04.917
and, with some hard work,

526
00:57:05.001 --> 00:57:07.754
I'm sure you'll eventually
be able to walk again.

527
00:57:10.173 --> 00:57:13.551
Now, I know it might not
sound like it right now but,

528
00:57:15.344 --> 00:57:17.138
given what happened,

529
00:57:18.514 --> 00:57:21.559
that makes you
a very lucky young man.

530
00:57:57.178 --> 00:57:58.888
Hey, Bob, come on!

531
00:58:36.008 --> 00:58:37.510
Hey, stranger.

532
00:58:42.098 --> 00:58:43.182
Hey.

533
00:58:44.934 --> 00:58:48.521
I heard you got out of the
hospital. How you doing?

534
00:58:52.149 --> 00:58:53.234
Okay.

535
00:58:59.156 --> 00:59:00.908
I thought about you.

536
00:59:05.287 --> 00:59:06.372
Yeah?

537
00:59:11.418 --> 00:59:13.212
Can I try something?

538
00:59:33.107 --> 00:59:34.441
Warm hands.

539
00:59:39.947 --> 00:59:41.031
Wow.

540
00:59:43.409 --> 00:59:44.827
Really warm.

541
00:59:47.830 --> 00:59:51.041
You ever hear of
the healing power of touch?

542
00:59:55.754 --> 00:59:56.755
No.

543
00:59:59.258 --> 01:00:02.428
But, at this point, I could
be talked into anything.

544
01:00:04.596 --> 01:00:06.807
I'm not coming on to you, Dan.

545
01:00:13.522 --> 01:00:16.859
Shouldn't you be healing
my leg instead of my chest?

546
01:00:19.903 --> 01:00:23.073
Maybe I don't think your

547
01:00:23.157 --> 01:00:25.576
leg is the only thing
that got broken.

548
01:00:36.211 --> 01:00:38.756
I know this is
a scary moment for you.

549
01:00:40.591 --> 01:00:42.885
Are you paying attention
to it?

550
01:00:47.055 --> 01:00:48.765
How is the old man?

551
01:00:50.893 --> 01:00:52.728
Why don't you ask him?

552
01:00:57.191 --> 01:00:58.984
He ever ask about me?

553
01:01:02.696 --> 01:01:04.156
That was bad.

554
01:01:04.907 --> 01:01:06.867
That was, like,
me sounding like...

555
01:01:06.909 --> 01:01:10.495
That was bad. That was you
sounding like you miss him.

556
01:01:16.585 --> 01:01:20.130
You know, he came
to visit you in the hospital.

557
01:01:28.263 --> 01:01:30.057
I'll see you around.

558
01:02:23.235 --> 01:02:24.611
Hey, Coach.

559
01:02:27.197 --> 01:02:28.448
Millman?

560
01:02:30.992 --> 01:02:32.786
Good to see you, man.

561
01:02:34.579 --> 01:02:37.582
Looks like you're bulked up
in the shoulders a little.

562
01:02:37.666 --> 01:02:41.169
That's pretty much all I can
do right now, presses and curls.

563
01:02:41.253 --> 01:02:42.504
Yeah.

564
01:02:44.339 --> 01:02:46.967
Hospital doesn't think so, but
I'm gonna be off this cane soon.

565
01:02:47.050 --> 01:02:48.426
Then, I'm back.

566
01:02:48.510 --> 01:02:50.470
You gotta listen to them.

567
01:02:50.512 --> 01:02:52.514
I have this crazy thought.

568
01:02:53.348 --> 01:02:56.059
I'm already gonna miss
the third round.

569
01:02:56.142 --> 01:02:57.769
I can't fix that.

570
01:02:59.312 --> 01:03:02.023
But that final qualifier?
Dan.

571
01:03:02.107 --> 01:03:04.109
That's not till next fall.

572
01:03:05.652 --> 01:03:07.988
That gives me eight months.

573
01:03:08.029 --> 01:03:10.991
What are you gonna do
in eight months?

574
01:03:11.032 --> 01:03:13.034
I already petitioned
the Olympic Committee.

575
01:03:13.118 --> 01:03:14.494
Dan, you have to be realistic.

576
01:03:14.578 --> 01:03:16.871
What if I get back? Huh?

577
01:03:16.955 --> 01:03:19.624
What if I get back to where I was?
You wouldn't want me on the team?

578
01:03:19.708 --> 01:03:22.002
Of course I would, Dan,
but look at yourself.

579
01:03:22.085 --> 01:03:26.464
For Christ's sake, you've got a piece
of metal holding your leg together!

580
01:03:27.048 --> 01:03:29.676
You can't give up on me.
I'm not giving up on you, Dan.

581
01:03:29.718 --> 01:03:31.845
Then, please, just hear me out. Dan!

582
01:03:36.808 --> 01:03:39.978
The doctors have told me
there's just no question.

583
01:03:41.396 --> 01:03:44.274
You will never
compete again.

584
01:05:28.670 --> 01:05:31.672
Christ, Millman, what the
hell is going on in there?

585
01:05:33.174 --> 01:05:35.927
Come on, Danny, open the door,
man! Answer me!

586
01:05:36.010 --> 01:05:37.303
Millman...

587
01:07:04.765 --> 01:07:06.392
What do you want?

588
01:07:27.997 --> 01:07:30.583
No one's stopping me,
so just stay away.

589
01:07:39.550 --> 01:07:40.926
I didn't come here
to stop you.

590
01:07:41.010 --> 01:07:42.761
You think I won't do it?

591
01:07:46.265 --> 01:07:48.309
'Cause I'm not afraid
of anything.

592
01:07:49.351 --> 01:07:50.769
Not even this.

593
01:07:53.856 --> 01:07:55.399
Or how about this?

594
01:07:59.320 --> 01:08:00.613
Or this?

595
01:08:06.410 --> 01:08:07.786
Look at you.

596
01:08:10.789 --> 01:08:12.958
Hanging on for dear life.

597
01:08:14.960 --> 01:08:16.462
Afraid to fall.

598
01:08:21.300 --> 01:08:22.635
Well, I say

599
01:08:23.677 --> 01:08:24.720
fall.

600
01:08:30.726 --> 01:08:33.228
It's not like
you're giving up anything.

601
01:08:34.271 --> 01:08:36.649
Nothing you haven't
already lost.

602
01:08:38.484 --> 01:08:43.739
What are you holding onto,
anyway?

603
01:08:53.582 --> 01:08:55.334
It's you, isn't it?

604
01:08:57.795 --> 01:09:00.297
You're the one
I have to let go of.

605
01:09:12.726 --> 01:09:14.812
You know what you're doing?

606
01:09:17.397 --> 01:09:18.398
No.

607
01:09:20.150 --> 01:09:21.944
Do you know

608
01:09:22.027 --> 01:09:23.737
who you are

609
01:09:24.279 --> 01:09:26.406
without me?

610
01:09:31.286 --> 01:09:32.329
No.

611
01:09:33.997 --> 01:09:35.582
Then what

612
01:09:35.666 --> 01:09:36.667
are

613
01:09:36.750 --> 01:09:38.544
you doing?

614
01:11:06.256 --> 01:11:07.257
Go.

615
01:11:15.891 --> 01:11:17.058
Again.

616
01:11:28.612 --> 01:11:30.739
I don't know what to do now.

617
01:11:31.781 --> 01:11:34.075
First realization
of a warrior.

618
01:11:35.452 --> 01:11:36.953
What is?

619
01:11:37.037 --> 01:11:38.455
Not knowing.

620
01:11:52.552 --> 01:11:54.471
What's happening to me?

621
01:11:57.390 --> 01:11:58.808
I don't cry.

622
01:12:00.018 --> 01:12:01.728
Apparently, you do.

623
01:12:05.065 --> 01:12:06.733
It's embarrassing.

624
01:12:10.612 --> 01:12:12.405
Emotions are natural,

625
01:12:13.782 --> 01:12:15.784
like the passing weather.

626
01:12:18.912 --> 01:12:20.580
What do you do

627
01:12:22.582 --> 01:12:24.959
if you can't do
what you were born to?

628
01:12:26.461 --> 01:12:28.713
Everything has
a purpose, Dan,

629
01:12:30.131 --> 01:12:31.466
even this.

630
01:12:35.929 --> 01:12:38.181
And it's up to you
to find it.

631
01:12:51.569 --> 01:12:52.570
Go.

632
01:13:01.538 --> 01:13:04.541
Your training can now move
to a new arena,

633
01:13:07.210 --> 01:13:12.507
an arena where you
find your answers from within.

634
01:13:14.592 --> 01:13:16.261
That old Plymouth.

635
01:13:17.303 --> 01:13:20.473
Sit on it till you have
something of value to tell me.

636
01:13:25.353 --> 01:13:26.646
That's it?

637
01:13:27.480 --> 01:13:31.317
I don't hear from you until you
have an insight worth sharing.

638
01:13:37.198 --> 01:13:38.575
That's all?

639
01:13:44.956 --> 01:13:46.749
How we doing tonight?

640
01:13:57.677 --> 01:13:58.803
Okay.

641
01:13:59.721 --> 01:14:01.139
Okay.

642
01:14:01.222 --> 01:14:04.684
Anger, hatred, violence,
they're really all just fear.

643
01:14:05.685 --> 01:14:09.230
Fear, then, not money,
is the root of all evil.

644
01:14:18.740 --> 01:14:23.453
Chaos Theory is correct except that
chaos is actually not chaotic at all

645
01:14:23.536 --> 01:14:25.663
but perfectly controlled.

646
01:14:25.747 --> 01:14:29.834
If you lend somebody $20 and never see
that person again, it was probably worth it.

647
01:14:30.877 --> 01:14:32.837
When making a peanut butter
and jelly sandwich,

648
01:14:32.920 --> 01:14:35.256
you must first apply the
peanut butter, not the jelly,

649
01:14:35.339 --> 01:14:37.425
to the bottom half
of the bread.

650
01:14:45.099 --> 01:14:50.062
The people that are the hardest to love
are usually the ones who need it the most.

651
01:14:53.483 --> 01:14:54.484
Hmm?

652
01:16:29.829 --> 01:16:32.289
There you are.
Thank you very much.

653
01:16:37.419 --> 01:16:39.713
There's never
nothing going on.

654
01:16:47.763 --> 01:16:50.015
There are no ordinary moments.

655
01:17:00.067 --> 01:17:01.527
Yeah.

656
01:17:06.782 --> 01:17:08.242
Welcome back.

657
01:17:18.210 --> 01:17:20.212
You gotta be kidding me.

658
01:17:24.174 --> 01:17:26.176
This isn't another vision,
is it?

659
01:17:26.260 --> 01:17:29.304
'Cause I don't see
how this could be happening.

660
01:17:32.516 --> 01:17:34.685
What the hell are you doing?

661
01:17:53.036 --> 01:17:54.621
Something wrong?

662
01:17:55.789 --> 01:17:59.376
We don't do this anymore,
remember? We know better.

663
01:18:00.627 --> 01:18:03.547
We're better than everyone
who doesn't know what we know

664
01:18:03.589 --> 01:18:05.924
or live the way we do?

665
01:18:06.008 --> 01:18:08.051
Is that what you mean?

666
01:18:08.135 --> 01:18:09.803
Not better, maybe.

667
01:18:11.263 --> 01:18:12.473
Smarter.

668
01:18:13.557 --> 01:18:15.350
There is no "better. "

669
01:18:19.938 --> 01:18:21.940
You will never be better.

670
01:18:22.774 --> 01:18:26.278
Same way you'll never be less
than anybody else.

671
01:18:32.618 --> 01:18:34.578
The habit is the problem.

672
01:18:35.954 --> 01:18:39.249
All you need to do is be
conscious about your choices

673
01:18:39.333 --> 01:18:41.668
and responsible
for your actions.

674
01:18:43.921 --> 01:18:48.383
Is that why, out of all the people
you could have taught, you chose me?

675
01:18:48.467 --> 01:18:50.636
You done flattering yourself?

676
01:18:55.223 --> 01:18:56.683
You chose me.

677
01:19:00.187 --> 01:19:02.189
Why should I believe you?

678
01:19:03.315 --> 01:19:06.485
You taught me yourself to only
listen to my own intuition.

679
01:19:06.568 --> 01:19:09.488
How do you know that I'm not
your own intuition

680
01:19:09.571 --> 01:19:11.615
speaking to you right now?

681
01:19:16.119 --> 01:19:18.288
You mean maybe
I made you up?

682
01:19:26.797 --> 01:19:28.965
Don't mess with me like that.

683
01:19:37.724 --> 01:19:42.020
Every what has its what? Every
action has its price and its pleasure.

684
01:19:42.104 --> 01:19:44.815
Recognizing both sides,
a warrior becomes...

685
01:19:44.856 --> 01:19:47.442
...realistic and responsible
for his actions.

686
01:19:49.611 --> 01:19:51.655
Boy sounds bad
over there, man.

687
01:19:54.282 --> 01:19:56.243
You gotta be kidding me.

688
01:19:56.868 --> 01:19:58.245
Money, boys.

689
01:19:59.079 --> 01:20:01.998
Picked the wrong guy
to pull this shit on, boys.

690
01:20:04.709 --> 01:20:08.004
Little leverage, at the right
time, at the right place?

691
01:20:11.466 --> 01:20:12.634
Yours.

692
01:20:14.261 --> 01:20:17.013
We can ramp this up
a little, tough guy.

693
01:20:22.602 --> 01:20:24.604
Thank you and good night.

694
01:20:26.898 --> 01:20:29.150
Didn't you forget our watches?

695
01:20:38.243 --> 01:20:41.037
This is where
you give it to them, right?

696
01:20:42.247 --> 01:20:45.750
Now, maybe I should have said
Dan's watch. I don't wear one.

697
01:20:48.295 --> 01:20:49.546
Give it.

698
01:20:55.760 --> 01:20:57.220
Thanks, old man.

699
01:20:57.303 --> 01:21:00.140
What are you, a medium jacket?

700
01:21:02.183 --> 01:21:03.685
Is he a what?

701
01:21:09.441 --> 01:21:11.317
I'm not taking your jacket.

702
01:21:11.401 --> 01:21:14.654
It's a good jacket.
Nice warm lining.

703
01:21:14.738 --> 01:21:16.197
I'll take it.

704
01:21:17.657 --> 01:21:19.242
It's a good jacket.

705
01:21:22.787 --> 01:21:25.582
You. You're about Dan's size.

706
01:21:39.345 --> 01:21:42.599
What size shoe do you
wear, Dan? Are you kidding?

707
01:21:43.808 --> 01:21:46.769
Christ, Soc, how far
are we gonna take this?

708
01:21:49.147 --> 01:21:50.648
They could have
killed us!

709
01:21:50.732 --> 01:21:52.567
They could have killed us!

710
01:21:53.735 --> 01:21:56.654
You could have kicked every
single one of those guys' asses.

711
01:21:56.738 --> 01:21:59.407
Instead, we're probably gonna get
picked up for indecent exposure.

712
01:21:59.490 --> 01:22:03.119
You think that's funny? Do
you? You think that's funny?

713
01:22:03.161 --> 01:22:06.080
You could have laid out every
single one of those guys.

714
01:22:06.122 --> 01:22:08.416
Tell me. Tell me what the
hell you were thinking.

715
01:22:08.499 --> 01:22:12.378
That the ones that are hardest to love
are the ones that need it the most.

716
01:22:12.462 --> 01:22:15.131
That knowledge
is not the same as wisdom.

717
01:22:15.173 --> 01:22:18.009
Wisdom is doing.
They could have killed us.

718
01:22:19.177 --> 01:22:21.095
It's a transformation.

719
01:22:22.639 --> 01:22:25.058
Death?
Yes.

720
01:22:25.141 --> 01:22:30.563
It's a little bit more radical than puberty
but nothing to get particularly upset about.

721
01:22:32.440 --> 01:22:34.942
What the hell
are you talking about?

722
01:22:36.319 --> 01:22:37.945
Death isn't sad.

723
01:22:39.572 --> 01:22:41.157
The sad thing is

724
01:22:42.241 --> 01:22:44.494
most people don't live at all.

725
01:22:53.127 --> 01:22:55.088
Is that a double double?

726
01:22:58.466 --> 01:23:01.094
No, that was a full twisting
double layout.

727
01:23:01.177 --> 01:23:03.638
I need to make it
a double double.

728
01:23:03.721 --> 01:23:05.139
Look at you.

729
01:23:06.432 --> 01:23:09.143
First day without
the training wheels.

730
01:23:09.185 --> 01:23:11.020
No cane, no crutches.

731
01:23:17.527 --> 01:23:19.862
Listen, I just came here
to say,

732
01:23:23.074 --> 01:23:25.868
I haven't always been
a very good friend.

733
01:23:28.913 --> 01:23:33.209
In fact, I can't remember the last
time I was somebody's good friend.

734
01:23:38.548 --> 01:23:40.508
Hey, it gets crazy,
you know?

735
01:23:41.759 --> 01:23:46.055
I mean, what are you gonna do when we're
always competing against each other?

736
01:23:48.516 --> 01:23:51.561
Anyway, what I really
came here to say was...

737
01:23:51.644 --> 01:23:53.479
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

738
01:23:53.563 --> 01:23:56.941
Trev, is Middleman apologizing?

739
01:23:58.109 --> 01:23:59.610
I think he is.

740
01:24:02.405 --> 01:24:05.533
Oh, God. Oh, God. He's
going down. Oh, my God.

741
01:24:05.616 --> 01:24:07.702
He's going down!
He's going down!

742
01:24:07.785 --> 01:24:11.163
Medic!
Get the paddles! Clear!

743
01:24:11.998 --> 01:24:13.416
Clear!

744
01:24:13.457 --> 01:24:16.544
Oh, God, take me instead!

745
01:24:16.794 --> 01:24:18.254
Oh, no!

746
01:24:18.337 --> 01:24:20.798
Took for granted
what I could do.

747
01:24:20.881 --> 01:24:22.883
I was sloppy with my life.

748
01:24:24.760 --> 01:24:26.262
I'm scared, but

749
01:24:27.430 --> 01:24:30.891
I feel like I got rid of
all the old stuff, and...

750
01:24:32.810 --> 01:24:34.937
I think it was
the right thing to do.

751
01:24:35.021 --> 01:24:36.772
When you feel fear,

752
01:24:41.736 --> 01:24:43.237
use the sword.

753
01:24:45.614 --> 01:24:48.451
Take it up here
and cut the mind to ribbons.

754
01:24:48.534 --> 01:24:51.245
Slash through
all those regrets and fears

755
01:24:51.287 --> 01:24:54.749
and anything else that lives
in the past or the future.

756
01:24:54.832 --> 01:24:57.042
I want to be able
to do that.

757
01:24:57.835 --> 01:25:00.045
I think I'm ready.

758
01:25:00.129 --> 01:25:01.630
Ready for what?

759
01:25:02.840 --> 01:25:05.593
Devoting my life
to a higher purpose.

760
01:25:05.634 --> 01:25:07.052
Really?

761
01:25:07.636 --> 01:25:09.597
Service to others, right?

762
01:25:12.808 --> 01:25:15.978
That's gonna be me, now. I'll
do whatever you think I should.

763
01:25:16.020 --> 01:25:17.730
All right.
All right.

764
01:25:17.813 --> 01:25:20.983
I think you should continue
your training as a gymnast.

765
01:25:36.123 --> 01:25:39.251
A warrior does not give up
what he loves, Dan.

766
01:25:40.502 --> 01:25:44.214
He finds the love
in what he does.

767
01:25:44.298 --> 01:25:45.674
Look at me!

768
01:25:47.343 --> 01:25:48.719
Look at me.

769
01:25:51.138 --> 01:25:54.516
I have a metal rod in my leg.

770
01:25:54.725 --> 01:25:57.311
A warrior
is not about perfection

771
01:25:57.353 --> 01:25:59.229
or victory

772
01:25:59.313 --> 01:26:01.065
or invulnerability.

773
01:26:02.358 --> 01:26:04.818
He's about
absolute vulnerability.

774
01:26:06.654 --> 01:26:08.197
That's the only
true courage.

775
01:26:08.280 --> 01:26:11.492
What kind of training you think I
could do? Huh? I just had an accident.

776
01:26:11.533 --> 01:26:14.870
The accident is your training.
Life is choice.

777
01:26:14.912 --> 01:26:17.873
You can choose to be a victim or
anything else you'd like to be.

778
01:26:17.915 --> 01:26:21.585
Just ignore what happened to me?
A warrior acts. Only a fool reacts.

779
01:26:21.668 --> 01:26:24.713
What if I can't do it? That's
the future. Throw it out.

780
01:26:24.797 --> 01:26:28.592
Well, how would we start? There
is no starting or stopping,

781
01:26:28.675 --> 01:26:30.052
only doing.

782
01:26:34.556 --> 01:26:36.809
I want to show you something.

783
01:26:52.449 --> 01:26:54.785
When did you do all this?

784
01:26:54.868 --> 01:26:57.454
When you were lying
in that hospital.

785
01:27:00.082 --> 01:27:01.708
While I was what?

786
01:27:09.341 --> 01:27:11.593
Now we can really
go to work.

787
01:30:01.679 --> 01:30:03.681
I don't believe you for
a minute. Seriously, man!

788
01:30:03.765 --> 01:30:07.018
You talking about that redhead? Not
the redhead, man, your redheaded girl.

789
01:30:07.102 --> 01:30:08.311
How is she my redheaded girl?

790
01:30:08.394 --> 01:30:10.480
You were on her all night,
bro. I handed her off to you.

791
01:30:10.563 --> 01:30:12.649
Which redhead
are we talking about?

792
01:30:16.236 --> 01:30:17.946
Make this a threesome?

793
01:30:22.242 --> 01:30:24.744
You're really not my type,
Middleman.

794
01:30:35.964 --> 01:30:40.802
What would you guys say if I told you I
was ready to get up on those rings again?

795
01:30:45.431 --> 01:30:48.101
I'd say you hit your head
and not your leg.

796
01:31:02.490 --> 01:31:03.825
Hey, Coach.

797
01:31:15.878 --> 01:31:17.255
That yours?

798
01:31:20.842 --> 01:31:22.176
Wait here.

799
01:31:38.609 --> 01:31:40.653
You boys give us the room
for a minute.

800
01:31:40.695 --> 01:31:43.573
What? Why?
What's going on?

801
01:31:45.241 --> 01:31:46.784
It's okay. Hey.

802
01:31:49.036 --> 01:31:51.873
I've had this in my office
for a few days now.

803
01:31:53.541 --> 01:31:56.377
I just didn't think I'd ever
need to give it to you.

804
01:31:57.044 --> 01:31:59.213
The Olympic Committee voted

805
01:31:59.297 --> 01:32:03.718
on your request for a special
dispensation to compete in the qualifiers.

806
01:32:06.262 --> 01:32:07.597
I'm sorry.

807
01:32:14.061 --> 01:32:15.980
You petitioned
the Olympic Committee?

808
01:32:16.063 --> 01:32:17.899
They talked to your doctors,

809
01:32:19.150 --> 01:32:23.905
who feel there's no evidence to indicate
that you're strong enough to compete.

810
01:32:28.326 --> 01:32:30.411
Is that what it says, Dan-o?

811
01:32:32.079 --> 01:32:33.164
No.

812
01:32:36.709 --> 01:32:39.086
It says that you could
turn that decision around

813
01:32:39.128 --> 01:32:41.714
if you saw any evidence
to the contrary.

814
01:32:43.466 --> 01:32:44.926
And I said I'm sorry.

815
01:32:45.009 --> 01:32:49.931
You watch me and you tell me
you don't see any evidence.

816
01:32:49.972 --> 01:32:53.351
I don't want to see a man who
was in a cast 10 months ago

817
01:32:53.434 --> 01:32:54.769
trying to do triple flips.

818
01:32:54.852 --> 01:32:57.271
Watch me.
Then you tell me that.

819
01:32:57.313 --> 01:33:00.608
The doctor said that you could spend
the rest of your life in a wheelchair.

820
01:33:00.650 --> 01:33:02.610
You think I care about that?

821
01:33:02.693 --> 01:33:06.280
No, Dan,
'cause I've seen your ego

822
01:33:06.364 --> 01:33:09.700
nearly kill you up on
those rings about 100 times

823
01:33:09.784 --> 01:33:13.287
and I am not ready
to see that happen for real.

824
01:33:18.250 --> 01:33:21.545
I've already said that
to the committee,

825
01:33:21.629 --> 01:33:23.839
and they have closed the case.

826
01:33:30.012 --> 01:33:31.680
You gave up on me.

827
01:33:38.395 --> 01:33:39.939
Danny, come on.

828
01:33:43.150 --> 01:33:44.819
You gave up on me.

829
01:33:48.239 --> 01:33:49.281
Dan.

830
01:34:08.342 --> 01:34:12.429
Nearly all of humanity
shares your predicament, Dan.

831
01:34:13.847 --> 01:34:16.725
If you don't get
what you want, you suffer.

832
01:34:19.019 --> 01:34:22.356
And even when you get
exactly what you want,

833
01:34:22.439 --> 01:34:24.441
you still suffer

834
01:34:24.525 --> 01:34:27.152
because you can't
hold onto it forever.

835
01:34:27.861 --> 01:34:29.697
He thought I couldn't do it.

836
01:34:29.780 --> 01:34:31.282
Doesn't matter.

837
01:34:31.365 --> 01:34:33.951
He doesn't know
that I'll be there 100%.

838
01:34:34.034 --> 01:34:37.913
You don't need him or any letter to get
up on those rings and do what you love.

839
01:34:37.997 --> 01:34:40.582
Yes, I do. All right?

840
01:34:40.666 --> 01:34:42.918
I'm talking about getting up there
and winning the gold right now,

841
01:34:43.002 --> 01:34:44.128
so, yes, I do.

842
01:34:44.211 --> 01:34:46.088
The gold is a craving.

843
01:34:46.171 --> 01:34:48.799
"If only I had it, I'd be happy.
" Can't you hear it in there?

844
01:34:48.882 --> 01:34:53.053
It's a dream, Soc. All right? I
can't think that dreams are bad.

845
01:34:53.095 --> 01:34:55.848
You don't surrender
your dreams, Dan.

846
01:34:56.890 --> 01:35:00.644
You surrender the one thing you
never have and you never will,

847
01:35:00.728 --> 01:35:01.937
control.

848
01:35:03.021 --> 01:35:06.024
Accept that you don't control
what will happen to you.

849
01:35:06.734 --> 01:35:10.904
That you may or you may not
compete in the Olympics.

850
01:35:11.655 --> 01:35:13.949
That you may
or you may not, Dan.

851
01:35:15.242 --> 01:35:19.037
And that you are something
exceptional either way.

852
01:35:20.414 --> 01:35:23.500
I was ready
to give this all up,

853
01:35:23.584 --> 01:35:25.711
but you stood here

854
01:35:25.752 --> 01:35:28.338
and you told me that you
wanted me to train again!

855
01:35:28.422 --> 01:35:30.299
I told you a warrior
does what he loves.

856
01:35:30.382 --> 01:35:33.177
And this is what I love!

857
01:35:33.260 --> 01:35:35.387
Chasing gold?

858
01:35:35.429 --> 01:35:38.599
Living in fear
that you might fail?

859
01:35:39.850 --> 01:35:40.934
That's what you love
about it?

860
01:35:41.018 --> 01:35:45.105
No! Dreaming of standing up
there and winning this thing!

861
01:35:45.189 --> 01:35:49.651
Of doing what has always felt like
the thing that I was put here to do.

862
01:35:49.735 --> 01:35:54.114
I've been on a trampoline since before
I could ride a bike because I loved it.

863
01:35:55.782 --> 01:35:58.118
'Cause it was the first thing

864
01:36:00.954 --> 01:36:04.249
that I was sure that I loved.

865
01:36:13.133 --> 01:36:14.468
I'm sorry.

866
01:36:16.678 --> 01:36:18.263
Okay? I'm sorry.

867
01:36:20.807 --> 01:36:24.269
I thought I was strong
but I'm not.

868
01:36:27.648 --> 01:36:30.859
'Cause I really tried
to give this whole thing up

869
01:36:35.739 --> 01:36:37.157
but I can't.

870
01:37:33.463 --> 01:37:37.133
Tomorrow morning,
bring your hiking shoes.

871
01:37:40.554 --> 01:37:46.142
I've got a place I've wanted to take you
since the first night you walked in here.

872
01:37:49.229 --> 01:37:51.731
It's a long hike
but I think...

873
01:37:53.733 --> 01:37:57.570
I think you're finally
ready to see it.

874
01:38:16.297 --> 01:38:17.841
Three?
Three.

875
01:38:20.260 --> 01:38:22.429
Life has just three rules?

876
01:38:22.512 --> 01:38:24.556
And you already know them.

877
01:38:25.724 --> 01:38:28.518
Paradox,

878
01:38:28.601 --> 01:38:29.894
humor and change.

879
01:38:30.603 --> 01:38:32.439
Paradox.

880
01:38:32.522 --> 01:38:36.359
Life is a mystery. Don't waste
time trying to figure it out.

881
01:38:37.652 --> 01:38:39.112
Humor.

882
01:38:39.154 --> 01:38:42.824
Keep a sense of humor,
especially about yourself.

883
01:38:42.907 --> 01:38:44.451
It is a strength
beyond all measure.

884
01:38:44.534 --> 01:38:45.744
Change.

885
01:38:53.793 --> 01:38:56.129
Know that nothing
stays the same.

886
01:39:02.469 --> 01:39:05.889
Hey, please tell me
we're getting a little closer.

887
01:39:12.187 --> 01:39:15.231
Come on, Soc,
it's been three hours, man.

888
01:39:15.315 --> 01:39:16.900
Now, we're here.

889
01:39:22.488 --> 01:39:25.325
We're where?
At what I came to show you.

890
01:39:31.789 --> 01:39:33.374
What, the view?

891
01:39:33.458 --> 01:39:35.460
There, next to your foot.

892
01:39:42.133 --> 01:39:43.635
The flower?
No.

893
01:39:43.718 --> 01:39:45.762
Better not be.
The rock.

894
01:39:50.850 --> 01:39:52.560
There's something...

895
01:39:52.644 --> 01:39:55.104
There's something special
about this rock?

896
01:39:55.188 --> 01:39:56.314
Something wrong?

897
01:39:56.397 --> 01:39:59.359
Come on, Soc! This is what
I was finally ready to see?

898
01:39:59.442 --> 01:40:02.070
Well, the whole trip up here,
you were excited, you were happy.

899
01:40:02.153 --> 01:40:03.738
Yeah, because I thought
I was gonna see something!

900
01:40:03.821 --> 01:40:07.075
You were like a kid on Christmas
morning. You said so yourself.

901
01:40:07.158 --> 01:40:09.035
The whole trip up here,
it made you feel good.

902
01:40:09.118 --> 01:40:12.455
Because for the past three hours I've
been waiting to see this wonderful thing.

903
01:40:12.538 --> 01:40:16.334
Well, what changed? That there's
nothing here but this rock!

904
01:40:18.461 --> 01:40:21.964
I probably should have told
you that before we left, huh?

905
01:40:23.007 --> 01:40:24.509
But I guess

906
01:40:27.053 --> 01:40:29.555
I wasn't sure
what we'd find, either.

907
01:40:31.557 --> 01:40:33.059
Never am.

908
01:40:39.649 --> 01:40:41.901
Sorry you're not
happy anymore.

909
01:40:55.998 --> 01:40:57.416
The journey.

910
01:41:06.259 --> 01:41:08.803
The journey's
what brings us happiness

911
01:41:10.388 --> 01:41:12.139
not the destination.

912
01:41:37.248 --> 01:41:38.541
Millman.

913
01:41:41.711 --> 01:41:43.504
Millman, what are you doing?

914
01:41:47.800 --> 01:41:50.594
Millman, get your hands
out of the chalk.

915
01:42:58.579 --> 01:42:59.663
Hey.

916
01:43:01.373 --> 01:43:02.416
Hey.

917
01:43:04.084 --> 01:43:05.878
Ready for the big day?

918
01:43:05.961 --> 01:43:08.130
Yeah. I leave tonight.

919
01:43:14.386 --> 01:43:16.013
Where you headed?

920
01:43:19.099 --> 01:43:21.060
Just out running.

921
01:43:21.101 --> 01:43:22.394
With a book?

922
01:43:24.438 --> 01:43:28.150
Actually, I think
I want to kiss you.

923
01:43:35.240 --> 01:43:36.867
Anything to say?

924
01:43:39.620 --> 01:43:41.372
Good luck tomorrow.

925
01:43:42.414 --> 01:43:45.334
You know, I see us together,
you and me.

926
01:43:46.585 --> 01:43:48.670
I dream stuff all the time!

927
01:43:49.922 --> 01:43:51.924
Sometimes it comes true!

928
01:43:56.929 --> 01:43:59.139
Hey, I'm just telling you!

929
01:43:59.223 --> 01:44:01.600
I really think
it might happen!

930
01:44:01.642 --> 01:44:03.435
Then maybe it will!

931
01:44:36.009 --> 01:44:38.011
This your place, Millman?

932
01:44:53.068 --> 01:44:56.238
Who are you?

933
01:44:56.321 --> 01:44:59.074
Where's the other guy
who works here?

934
01:44:59.324 --> 01:45:01.034
I just started today.

935
01:45:03.704 --> 01:45:06.498
You want gas,
you gotta pump it yourself.

936
01:45:08.041 --> 01:45:09.126
Hey.

937
01:45:12.838 --> 01:45:14.172
Hey, man.

938
01:45:26.184 --> 01:45:27.310
Hello!

939
01:45:52.377 --> 01:45:55.380
Where's your secret weapon?
I don't know.

940
01:45:57.174 --> 01:46:00.844
What do you mean? He stood you
up? We moving on, here, Millman?

941
01:46:10.061 --> 01:46:12.898
He ever tell you
how he got up on that roof?

942
01:46:16.193 --> 01:46:17.861
It doesn't matter.

943
01:46:47.140 --> 01:46:50.477
A very strong 9.3
for young David Bloodgood,

944
01:46:50.560 --> 01:46:53.897
ranking him in the top seven athletes
we've seen competing here today.

945
01:46:53.938 --> 01:46:55.940
The competition
is fierce this year.

946
01:46:55.982 --> 01:46:59.152
I can't remember a time when
the bar has been raised so high.

947
01:46:59.235 --> 01:47:00.570
And for good reason, Bart.

948
01:47:00.612 --> 01:47:02.238
For those of you
just joining our broadcast,

949
01:47:02.280 --> 01:47:06.409
these trials today will decide the
six young men from all over the country

950
01:47:06.493 --> 01:47:10.663
who will be representing the United
States at this year's Olympics.

951
01:47:14.667 --> 01:47:18.588
All right, Millman. Just the
routine you showed me. Right?

952
01:47:20.673 --> 01:47:24.260
No triple flips,
no showboating.

953
01:47:25.386 --> 01:47:27.639
Just get up there and be you.

954
01:47:32.185 --> 01:47:35.897
Coming up next, the top
qualifiers from UC Berkeley.

955
01:47:38.399 --> 01:47:39.484
Hey.

956
01:47:42.821 --> 01:47:45.281
How you doing?
You together?

957
01:47:49.077 --> 01:47:51.704
You did something that none of us
can completely wrap our heads around.

958
01:47:51.788 --> 01:47:53.456
You know that, right?

959
01:47:56.000 --> 01:47:58.670
I mean, it's like a miracle
or something, Dan-o.

960
01:48:02.173 --> 01:48:04.634
Whatever you learned, man,

961
01:48:04.717 --> 01:48:07.053
whatever that guy
taught you...

962
01:48:09.722 --> 01:48:11.140
You think...

963
01:48:14.143 --> 01:48:17.438
You think maybe you can rub a
little of that magic onto me?

964
01:48:20.525 --> 01:48:22.360
It's not magic, Tommy.

965
01:48:24.195 --> 01:48:27.865
Just getting rid of all that
bullshit you have up in your head,

966
01:48:27.949 --> 01:48:30.368
tells you
you might not be enough.

967
01:48:33.830 --> 01:48:35.790
So when you get up there,

968
01:48:38.126 --> 01:48:40.628
you make every move
about the move.

969
01:48:42.171 --> 01:48:44.549
All right?
Not about the gold.

970
01:48:44.632 --> 01:48:47.468
Not about what your dad
thinks about you.

971
01:48:47.552 --> 01:48:49.303
Not about anything

972
01:48:51.514 --> 01:48:53.641
but that one moment in time.

973
01:48:57.103 --> 01:48:59.147
But this is for the gold.

974
01:49:02.567 --> 01:49:04.736
Everything we do, Dan-o.

975
01:49:04.819 --> 01:49:06.028
I mean, at least for me,

976
01:49:06.070 --> 01:49:10.408
my whole life is about getting those
20 seconds in front of those judges

977
01:49:10.491 --> 01:49:12.743
so they can
give me that gold.

978
01:49:15.580 --> 01:49:19.417
You wanna know what my dad would
think of me if that happened?

979
01:49:20.543 --> 01:49:23.713
You want to know how
my whole life would change?

980
01:49:23.754 --> 01:49:27.842
How everything that's a problem
right now wouldn't matter anymore?

981
01:49:28.759 --> 01:49:30.761
I'd get everything I want.

982
01:49:34.765 --> 01:49:36.517
I'd get to be happy.

983
01:49:39.562 --> 01:49:41.647
I'd get to be happy, Dan-o.

984
01:49:46.152 --> 01:49:48.821
Next up,
ladies and gentlemen,

985
01:49:48.905 --> 01:49:53.451
from UC Berkeley, Dan Millman.

986
01:49:53.534 --> 01:49:57.246
Now, Dan is quite the wild card, Bart,
because less than 10 short months ago,

987
01:49:57.288 --> 01:50:01.459
this young man actually shattered
his leg in a motorcycle accident.

988
01:53:03.849 --> 01:53:05.601
Where are you, Dan?

989
01:53:07.394 --> 01:53:08.812
Here.

990
01:53:08.854 --> 01:53:11.190
What time is it?

991
01:53:11.273 --> 01:53:13.233
Now.

992
01:53:13.317 --> 01:53:14.902
What are you?

993
01:53:16.695 --> 01:53:18.113
This moment.
